      "message": "Overall, I am cleaning up some of the tech debt on libselinux.\n\nThrough our discussions, we realized that libselinux was both present in LL-NDK and VNDK (it should be either but not both). The second change here is to remove the VNDK altogether (actually finish the removal, as this was started in a previous commit). \n\nThis change is about preparing the eventual removal of some deprecated functions. We\u0027d like to keep the current behavior for anything linking at R and S, but for T, a warning/error is displayed to indicate that the function is not doing anything. Feel free to comment on the bug as well if you think we should have a different approach here. Thanks.",
